Program runs

Here, you manually create the .class file.

Example:

javac Hello.java
java Hello

<!-- Case 2: You directly run the .java file -->

With modern Java versions, you can do:
java Hello.java

In this case, Java does something like:
Hello.java
   │
   │ java command internally compiles it
   ▼
Temporary/In-memory bytecode
   │
   ▼
JVM executes it

So even though you did not run javac yourself, Java still compiles the source code before executing it.
You have JDK 25, so this feature is available  



Java Code Execution — Complete Explanation

Let's take the complete flow and understand what happens at each stage, why it happens, and how it connects to the next stage.




                    JAVA CODE EXECUTION

1. WRITE CODE
       │
       ▼
   Main.java
       │
       ▼
2. COMPILE
   javac Main.java
       │
       ▼
   Lexical Analysis
       ↓
   Syntax Analysis
       ↓
   Semantic Analysis
       ↓
   Bytecode Generation
       │
       ▼
   Main.class
   (Bytecode)
       │
       ▼
3. RUN
   java Main
       │
       ▼
4. JVM STARTS
       │
       ▼
5. CLASS LOADING
       │
       ├── Loading
       │
       ├── Linking
       │     ├── Verification
       │     ├── Preparation
       │     └── Resolution
       │
       └── Initialization
             ├── Static Variables
             └── Static Blocks
       │
       ▼
6. main() STARTS
       │
       ▼
7. STACK FRAME CREATED
       │
       ├── Local Variables
       └── Operand Stack
       │
       ▼
