Quick revision in one sentence

Java source code is compiled by javac into bytecode; the JVM loads and prepares the required classes, initializes them, creates stack frames to execute methods, uses the interpreter and JIT compiler to execute bytecode as native instructions, sends results to the CPU and output system, and finally terminates when the program's non-daemon threads have finished.